{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa: Dinner for Four"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Kitchen Tales"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Looking to the Stars > Indira Gandhi"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Identify and describe personal and regional eating habits and cooking in a range of communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le03ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressing quantity with food"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "To talk about specific food quantities and weights we following measures are used throughout North America."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Measurements (Nouns)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Amount\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"pound (lb)<br />  pint (pt)<br /> quart (qt)<br /> ounce (oz)<br />  gallon (gal)<br /> dozen\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a little less than half a kilogram at 454 g<br /> a little less than half a liter<br /> a little less than one liter<br /> almost 30 ml or 30 grams;  8 oz = 250 ml = 1 measuring cup<br /> a little less than 4 liters<br /> 12 pieces\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "In English, we use words we call <span class=\"strong\">quantifiers</span> to talk about undefined quantities. These words are also often used with food. We use different quantifiers depending on whether the noun is <span class=\"strong\">countable</span> or <span class=\"strong\">uncountable</span>."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":5,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Large Quantities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Small Quantities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Zero Quantities\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"More Than You Need\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Countable</span><br>Lots of (+)<br>Not many (-)<br>How many?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(+) a lot of<br>plenty of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(a) few<br>very few\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not ... any<br>none (in short answers)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"too many\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Uncountable</span><br>Lots of (+)<br>Not much<br>How much?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(+) a lot of<br>plenty of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(a) little<br>very little\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"not ... any<br>none (in short answers)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"too much\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you pass me a little salt, please?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I need to boil a few eggs for the spinach salad."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm full. I ate too much pizza!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I baked plenty of muffins for everyone plus brownies to top off our meal!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have very little icing left for all these cake layers."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have plenty of room in the sink to drain the fat from the pan."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " What did you use to do?"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " \"<span class=\"strong\">Used to</span>\u201d and \u201c<span class=\"strong\">would</span>\u201d express a pattern of action that occurred regularly in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "But: <br/>Only \"<span class=\"strong\">used to</span>\" expresses repeated habits in the past. <br/>Only \"<span class=\"strong\">would</span>\" is more formal and sentimental."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> + verb in basic form (infinitive) + complement\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> + verb in basic form (infinitive) + complement\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My mom <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">teach</span> me how to cook.<br/>   I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">used to</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">spend</span> more time cooking but not anymore.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">have</span> lasagna on every holiday.<br/> My grandfather <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">read</span> us stories after dinner.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How did you use to get to school before you got a bicycle?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to get up really early to take the bus."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to get up early, and I would take my bike out of the locker, put on my helmet, and I would ride all the way to school."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Lasagna used to be a staple in our home."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We used to line the cake trays with wax paper so it wouldn't stick."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "lasagna"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an Italian dish made of ground beef and cheese between layers of pasta noodles "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sally wanted Vanessa to teach her to make lasagna."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about cooking."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "attention to detail"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to give special care to the details in a task "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To make a good lasagna requires attention to detail."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to soak"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something very wet with water"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You don't have to soak the lasagna noodles on water before cooking."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "moisture"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small amount of liquid that makes something wet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The dry lasagna noodles absorb the moisture from the other ingredients."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le03ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ground beef"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "Beef that has been grou